Deployment-level country selection (VPNGATE_COUNTRY / VPNGATE_COUNTRY_LOCK).

docker-compose.yml can pin the node pool to a country:

    environment:
      - VPNGATE_COUNTRY=JP        # ISO alpha-2 code, or a name ("日本" / "Japan")

With a single country the routing mode is additionally locked to it
(routing_mode=fixed_region), so the app only ever connects to the best node
*inside* that country and the background prober only measures its nodes.
Several countries (VPNGATE_COUNTRY=JP,KR) narrow the candidate pool without
locking the region; VPNGATE_COUNTRY_LOCK=0 keeps the pool filter only and
leaves other countries available as a fallback. Unsetting the variable restores
panel-driven routing.

apply_country_env() is called from load_ui_config(), so the environment wins
over the persisted ui_auth.json on every load and the panel shows the enforced
values in 路由设置 / 节点国家筛选.

